0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z04-S01","name":"Zone IV · Scene 1: Labors of the Field — The Thrice-Ploughed Fallow","zone":"Z04","lines":"18.541–549","greek":"Ἐν δ᾽ ἐτίθει νειὸν μαλακὴν, πίειραν ἄρουραν, εὐρεῖαν τρίπολον· πολλοὶ δ᾽ ἀροτῆρες ἐν αὐτῇ ζεύγεα δινεύοντες ἐλάστρεον ἔνθα καὶ ἔνθα... ἡ δὲ μελαίνετο ὄπισθεν, ἀρηρομένῃ δὲ ἐῴκει χρυσείη περ ἐοῦσα· τὸ δὴ περὶ θαῦμα τέτυκτο.","buckley":"On it he also placed a soft fallow field, rich glebe, wide, thrice-ploughed; and in it many ploughmen drove hither and thither, turning round their teams. But when, returning, they reached the end of the field, then a man, advancing, gave into their hands a cup of very sweet wine; but they turned themselves in series, eager to reach the other end of the deep fallow. But it grew black behind, and was like unto ploughed land, though being golden; which was a very great marvel.","worldModel":{"vision":"Golden field plates (297) progressively flipping to black (0) and dark-brown (308) furrowed tiles behind the bronze ploughshare.","memory":"Iterative loop with state mutation: drive furrow → reach headland → receive cup of sweet wine (δέπας μελιηδέος οἴνου) → turn team → golden metal turns black behind (μελαίνετο).","controller":"Homer’s supreme neurosymbolic marvel (περὶ θαῦμα τέτυκτο): material gold executing the optical state-change of dark earth."}}

